    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">As approved in Docket No. CP22-468, on September 30, 2024, Trailblazer abandoned 324 miles of pipeline, associated interconnects, and three compressor stations.&#160; Additionally, Trailblazer abandoned the remaining additional 68 miles of pipeline on December 24, 2024.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Transferred to Account No. 211, Miscellaneous Paid-in Capital.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Transferred to Account No. 211, Miscellaneous Paid-in Capital.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">General Plant reported does not include an allocation of corporate facilities to or from Tallgrass Energy Partners, LP ("TEP") and affiliates.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents under collections pursuant to Trailblazer&#8217;s tariff fuel/power tracking mechanisms.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents the Annual Charge Adjustment ("ACA"), which is an annual fee charged by the FERC and recovered from the shippers.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents over collections pursuant to Trailblazer&#8217;s tariff fuel/power tracking mechanisms.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In 2024, Trailblazer abandoned approximately $71 million (NBV) of utility assets and reclassified them as non-utility assets. In February 2025, the assets were transferred through internal Tallgrass affiliate transactions and ultimately placed into Trailblazer CO&#8322; Pipeline, LLC, with Trailblazer selling them to Tallgrass Energy Ventures (TEV) for $71.4 million. Following the transaction, Trailblazer re-evaluated its ownership percentage, tax rates, and apportionment factors and subsequently noted a decrease in its composite state tax rate from 26.14% to 23.087%. This change resulted in a reduction of deferred tax assets, which was recorded in Account 254.3 (Other Regulatory Liabilities) as well as increase in regulatory asset, Account 182, both are being amortized to Account 410.1 (Provision for Deferred Income Taxes) over the remaining useful life of the assets.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote"/>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In accordance with the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act signed into law on December 22, 2017, Trailblazer remeasured its accumulated deferred income taxes (Accounts 190 and 282) during the year ended December 31, 2017 based on the new tax rates, resulting in a decrease in the net deferred tax liability. The adjustment to Trailblazer's accumulated deferred income taxes was recorded in Account 254. The balance is amortized to Account 410.1, Provision of Deferred Income Taxes, over the estimated remaining useful life of the pipeline.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents over collections pursuant to Trailblazer&#8217;s tariff fuel/power tracking mechanisms.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents over collections pursuant to Trailblazer&#8217;s tariff fuel/power tracking mechanisms.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Shipper Refunds pursuant to the Tariff Revenue Crediting Mechanism.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Fuel recovery volumes (shipper supplied gas for transmission): 89,696 dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Fuel recovery volumes (shipper supplied gas for transmission): 118,942 dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Fuel recovery volumes (shipper supplied gas for transmission): 95,506 dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Park and loan service volumes report net:&#160; 0 dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Park and loan service volumes report net: 0 dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Park and loan service volumes report net:0 dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The electric power cost used in compressor station operations was $26,000</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Many of the natural gas volumes required to be reported on this page are tracked at the entity level, rather than by service type (i.e. firm transport, interruptible transport, etc.) or by discounted, negotiated, or recourse rate contracts and, therefore, the amounts reported have been allocated to the service types and to discounted, negotiated or recourse rate contracts based on reasonable assumptions.</link:footnote>
